			"notes": "First public release of wUtilities.\n\nwUtilities lets a server restrict selected features in compatible wWorldMap and wWaypoints clients while allowing players without those mods to join normally.\n\n- wWorldMap: disable the entire mod, player radar, entity radar, Orbit, or cave mode.\n- wWaypoints: disable the entire mod, non-vanilla sneak behavior, or sign-popup suppression. Basic Toggle Sneak and its indicator remain available under the narrower sneak restriction.\n- Server policy is connection-scoped and does not overwrite players' saved preferences.\n- Both policy channels use protocol version 1, including native Forge and NeoForge negotiation.\n\nChoose the JAR for your server loader and Minecraft version. The release contains a Bukkit-family JAR, combined Fabric/Quilt cohort JARs, and separate Forge and NeoForge JARs. See the platform guide for supported versions and dependencies:\nhttps://github.com/wSmoothie/wUtilities/blob/main/documentation/PLATFORMS.md\n\nConfiguration is generated on first startup:\n- Bukkit-family servers: `plugins/wUtilities/wutilities.properties`\n- Fabric, Quilt, Forge, and NeoForge: `config/wutilities.properties`\n\nEdit the file and restart the server to apply a new policy. Existing legacy wWorldMapUtils configuration is copied forward automatically.\r\n\nVerification: all 29 artifacts were built with the target checks enabled. Startup, default configuration generation, and restriction configuration after restart were checked across all 72 defined version/platform targets, plus Spigot 1.20.1 and 26.2. Network probes on Minecraft 1.21.11 covered policy delivery, reconnects, plain-client admission, and native Forge/NeoForge version-1 negotiation (22 cases, 46 connections). These checks do not establish client gameplay or Folia multi-region behavior on every version.\n\nMinecraft 26.3 additions (wUtilities 0.1.0):\n- Combined Fabric/Quilt artifact; Fabric Loader 0.19.3+ or Quilt Loader 0.30.1+, with Fabric API for 26.3.\n- Native NeoForge artifact, built against NeoForge 26.3.0.46-beta.\n- Native Forge artifact, built against Forge 66.0.9.\n- The existing Bukkit 1.20+ JAR also supports 26.3 on available Bukkit-family servers.\n- Minecraft 26.3 requires Java 25.\n\nVerification for these additions: all 32 artifacts passed the complete build, automated tests, and applicable metadata checks. Minecraft 26.3 packaged-artifact startup, unrestricted default configuration, and configured restrictions after restart passed on Fabric, Quilt, NeoForge, Forge, Paper, Purpur, and Leaf (7 targets, 14 launches). The tested JAR hashes matched the published artifacts; every disposable server directory was removed. These checks do not establish player joins, network policy delivery, client gameplay, or Folia multi-region behavior."
		}
